Date:    Thu, 28 Jan 1993 17:55:23 -0800 (PST)
From: GRAPS@galileo.arc.nasa.gov
Subject: TECH: Magneto-Optical Drive, a Review

Tim May writes:

>* Bernoulli, by Iomega. Very rugged, very fast. But nonstandard. Drive
>cost is $500 for a 90 MB and $800 for a 150 MB. Cartridges are fairly
>expensive, at about $120 for the 90s and $140 for the 150s.

It may be nonstandard, but it has something else going for it that
you didn't mention. You can use the same Bernoulli Transportable 
MultiDisk 90 or 150 on different systems: PC, Mac, Suns, SGI's, etc. 
Some software for file transfer between the platforms is necessary which 
you can buy extra for a few hundred dollars.
 
I've convinced my boss at work to get one of these so that we can use the same
cartridges and drive between my SGI workstation and my Mac at work and
thereby saving ourselves alot of time sending/converting data between
the different machines. I hope to buy one of these eventually for
my home Mac too so that I can work with larger data files at home.


Amara Graps
graps@gal.arc.nasa.gov




